*.sh text eol=lf
# Licence text: kept byte-identical to the FSF source (LF line endings)
LICENSE text eol=lf

# Generated notices (compared byte for byte by validate.sh)
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md text eol=lf

# Animated renders for the documentation and README (DOCUMENTATION/assets/, .github/readme/).
# Git already detects them as binary, but this is explicit on purpose: a single line-ending
# substitution corrupts the file, and the rule must survive a future `* text=auto`.
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.gif binary
